# Wake-fleet scripts

- Import bots from `roster.ts` (`rosterBots`, `findBot`, `resolveOwner`, `readOwnership`). A pasted name table is a bug.
- `fleet-status.ts` may read grind logs and `events.log` only for supply, repeat, recovery, and pathfinding detectors. Job identity is the roster command. Ownership is written by `BotSDK.connect`, not by matching a name in argv.
- `grindTail` must stay a bounded tail read. Do not `readFileSync` the whole log.
- Do not write `assignment.json` from fleet-status or fleet-launchd. `BotSDK.connect` (control mode) records ownership. Do not bring back `inferCommand()`, `resolveCommand()`, or `writeAssignment()`.
- `watch-fleet.sh` panes come from `roster.ts tmux`. Do not hardcode Jackpoo / ABGARMY towers again.
- `install` / `restart` must rewrite plists from the current roster; keep installed argv in lockstep with `roster.json`.
- Grind appends go through `appendGrindLog` (`sdk/grind-log.ts`). `ActivitySession.log` already does. Do not switch it back to unbounded `appendFileSync`.
